{
  "name": "Spinal Fusion Use Case",
  "description": "Reconstruction of asaree-spinal-use-case/spinal_pipeline.ipynb as an ASAREE protocol: SF-DC -> SF-FTE -> SF-FS -> SF-MLM, each gated by a Critic Gate, all sharing one Azure Foundry LLM connector whose model/effort are experimental factors, plus a shared 'Critic enabled' factor gating all four stages at once. BEFORE running: (1) register the 6 asaree-sklearn-* MCP servers under your own account via the use case's register_servers.py -- this file's MCP Tool nodes have server_id left null (server ids are per-account) and will show 'Select a server...' until you manually reselect the matching server_name in each Tool node's inspector; reselecting currently resets that node's own tool allow-list to 'all tools' for that server, so re-narrow it back down using the tool_names noted in each Tool node's label; (2) register the dataset and attach it via PATCH /experiments/{id} (dataset_id isn't part of this file); (3) note that ASAREE's generic executor has no equivalent of the notebook's per-cell on-disk workspace versioning (v1_dc/v2_fte/v3_fs handoff) or its direct, non-agent scoring tool call on asaree-sklearn-model -- importing this file reproduces the DESIGN faithfully, but a 'Run all cells' will not reproduce a real end-to-end scored run without those two pieces being added or driven manually. See the chat summary for the full gap list.",
